recommendations.why:
Recyclers retype the same purchases and sales into each CPCB portal, and the portals reject back-dated rows and forbid edits. Exports should follow each portal's fields and date order:
- e-waste purchases by item code;
- tyre purchases (supplier, address, source, tonnes, invoice number, optional GSTIN, date);
- plastic sale e-invoice fields (GSTINs, IRN, HSN code, amount);
- battery quarterly Form 4 totals.

This saves hours each quarter and needs no CPCB API.

risks:
Partners' exposure: over-claiming leads to one of the following:
- a 1-year bar for plastic processors;
- e-waste registration revoked for up to 3 years;
- permanent revocation for used-oil recyclers on a third offence;
- prosecution under section 15 of the Environment Protection Act.
Any data-quality failure on Luma.Green becomes a partner's legal problem.
